{"nodes": [{"id": "drive_the_method_materials_rewrite_chapter6_what_lambda_is_chapter6", "label": "Chapter 6 \u2014 What \u039b is: distributive, modular, Sperner", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "drive/The Method Materials/REWRITE-chapter6-what-lambda-is.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "drive_the_method_materials_rewrite_chapter6_what_lambda_is_distributive", "label": "\u039b is distributive \u2014 a sublattice of a product of chains", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "drive/The Method Materials/REWRITE-chapter6-what-lambda-is.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The least surprising fact in the chapter and the most load-bearing: distributivity is what admits Birkhoff's representation."}, {"id": "drive_the_method_materials_rewrite_chapter6_what_lambda_is_modular_rank", "label": "Rank is conserved \u2014 rank(a\u2228b) + rank(a\u2227b) = rank(a) + rank(b), zero violations on 475,800 pairs", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "drive/The Method Materials/REWRITE-chapter6-what-lambda-is.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Strictly stronger than the submodularity of matroid rank or entropy; the equality is the signature of distributivity, and the pairwise test finds a distributivity failure in half the work of the triple test."}, {"id": "drive_the_method_materials_rewrite_chapter6_what_lambda_is_seventeen_generators", "label": "Seventeen join-irreducibles, twenty covering relations \u2014 a 57-fold compression", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "drive/The Method Materials/REWRITE-chapter6-what-lambda-is.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The covers are the physics made visible: shell before subshell before occupancy, and a target subshell requiring its shell. The patterns hold at fifteen across six cap settings, which is what licenses stating the poset once."}, {"id": "drive_the_method_materials_rewrite_chapter6_what_lambda_is_sperner", "label": "Sperner \u2014 largest antichain equals largest rank level, 122 at rank 11", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "drive/The Method Materials/REWRITE-chapter6-what-lambda-is.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The rank sequence is log-concave hence unimodal, so Sperner holds as a consequence rather than by coincidence."}, {"id": "drive_the_method_materials_rewrite_chapter6_what_lambda_is_not_rank_symmetric", "label": "\u039b is not rank-symmetric and not self-dual \u2014 skew \u22120.43, 8 of 976 survive reflection", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "drive/The Method Materials/REWRITE-chapter6-what-lambda-is.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Low ranks are cut by floors and high ranks by caps; there are more caps than floors, so the skew measures how much more Pauli constrains than counting does."}, {"id": "drive_the_method_materials_rewrite_chapter6_what_lambda_is_particle_hole", "label": "The reflection restricted to one occupancy coordinate is particle\u2013hole conjugation", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "drive/The Method Materials/REWRITE-chapter6-what-lambda-is.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "drive_the_method_materials_rewrite_chapter6_what_lambda_is_constraint_graph_tree", "label": "The constraint graph is a tree \u2014 three consequences", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "drive/The Method Materials/REWRITE-chapter6-what-lambda-is.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "No sieve, a recoverable order, and no redundancy: there is exactly one path between any two coordinates, so two-route self-defence cannot come from the constraints and must come from derived quantities."}, {"id": "drive_the_method_materials_rewrite_chapter6_what_lambda_is_order_dimension_8", "label": "Order dimension exactly 8 \u2014 the width of the poset of join-irreducibles", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "drive/The Method Materials/REWRITE-chapter6-what-lambda-is.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "drive_the_method_materials_rewrite_chapter6_what_lambda_is_figure_6_1", "label": "Figure 6.1 \u2014 the seventeen join-irreducibles and their twenty covers", "file_type": "image", "source_file": "drive/The Method Materials/REWRITE-chapter6-what-lambda-is.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "drive_the_method_materials_rewrite_chapter6_what_lambda_is_figure_6_2", "label": "Figure 6.2 \u2014 the rank sequence, log-concave and asymmetric", "file_type": "image", "source_file": "drive/The Method Materials/REWRITE-chapter6-what-lambda-is.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}], "edges": [{"source": "drive_the_method_materials_rewrite_chapter6_what_lambda_is_chapter6", "target": "drive_the_method_materials_rewrite_chapter6_what_lambda_is_distributive", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "drive/The Method Materials/REWRITE-chapter6-what-lambda-is.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "drive_the_method_materials_rewrite_chapter6_what_lambda_is_chapter6", "target": "drive_the_method_materials_rewrite_chapter6_what_lambda_is_modular_rank", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "drive/The Method Materials/REWRI